      "text": [
        " كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ (صلى الله عليه وآله) يَقْسِمُ لَحَظَاتِهِ بَيْنَ أَصْحَابِهِ يَنْظُرُ إِلَى ذَا وَ يَنْظُرُ إِلَى ذَا بِالسَّوِيَّةِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "<a id=\"_Toc492473523\">H 14841</a> – Narrated to me Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Umar Bin Abdul Aziz, from Jameel, who has said:",
          "<span class=\"first-chapter-phrase\"><span class=\"first-in-chapter character-a\">A</span>bu Abdullah</span><sup>asws</sup> has said: ‘The Rasool Allah<sup>saww</sup> used to divide his<sup>saww</sup> moments between his<sup>saww</sup> companions. He<sup>saww</sup> would look at this one, and look at that one equally’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "394. Narrated to me Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Umar Bin Abdul Aziz, from Jameel, who has said: Abu Abdullah (a.s.) has said: ‘The Rasool Allah (saww) used to divide his (saww) moments between his (saww) companions. He (saww) would look at this one, and look at that one equally’."
        ]
      }
